## P1. Does an old tell reach a session started later? (README: "A session started later doesn't get it."; row 92 (b): "a session given a role later never gets an old tell")

### P1a. The session that was told ends before its turn does; a new session takes the role later (3 s later here; the next morning, in life)

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-night CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role implementer
You are now implementer in repo1.
# s-night is in the middle of a turn: it has the role and no listener yet

$ [terminal] handoff fyi Carry on while I'm away. Merge when the reviewer approves.
told implementer (#1)
not told, no session: reviewer, reviewer-2
# exit 0

# s-night's process has ended (a crash, a usage limit, a closed window). It never listened, so it never read the tell.

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-morning CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role implementer
You are now implementer in repo1.

# the bindings now, and the tell's time:
{"v":1,"role":"implementer","session":"s-morning","pid":<pid>,"since":"2026-11-11T00:20:19Z"}
"ts":"2026-11-11T00:20:16Z","kind":"fyi"

$ echo '{"session_id":"s-morning","hook_event_name":"Stop"}' | env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-morning CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff hook listen --timeout 5s
handoff: nothing new for implementer in 5s. Just end your turn; listening starts again when it ends.
# exit 2
# ^ the new session's first listen: exit 2 wakes it with the old tell. The line names no time.

### P1b. The operator moves the role to another session before the first one's turn ends

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-one CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role reviewer
You are now reviewer in repo2.

$ [terminal] handoff fyi Carry on while I'm away.
told reviewer (#1)
not told, no session: implementer, reviewer-2
# exit 0

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-two CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role reviewer
You are now reviewer in repo2. Another session had reviewer; it has no role now.

$ echo '{"session_id":"s-two","hook_event_name":"Stop"}' | env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-two CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff hook listen --timeout 5s
handoff: nothing new for reviewer in 5s. Just end your turn; listening starts again when it ends.
# exit 2

### P1c. A Codex thread that took its role by a command and ran no hook: its binding has no process, so it counts as a session for good

$ env CODEX_THREAD_ID=t-gone handoff role reviewer
You are now reviewer in repo3.
{"v":1,"role":"reviewer","session":"t-gone","since":"2026-11-11T00:20:30Z"}
# no such thread runs. The tell still says it told reviewer:

$ [terminal] handoff fyi Carry on while I'm away.
told reviewer (#1)
not told, no session: implementer, reviewer-2
# exit 0

$ env CODEX_THREAD_ID=t-new handoff role reviewer
You are now reviewer in repo3. Another session had reviewer; it has no role now.

$ handoff wait --for reviewer --timeout 2s
# exit 3

